WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:02.849
The opening canvas is an interactive assembly.

2
00:00:02.849 --> 00:00:07.733
Assemble the components into an application, separate them, or inspect the wireframe.

3
00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:10.989
Select a piece and change its corner radius.

4
00:00:10.989 --> 00:00:15.873
On a phone, the picker shows one component at a readable size.

5
00:00:15.873 --> 00:00:17.501
The catalog follows below.

6
00:00:18.001 --> 00:00:28.054
The workspace puts the code editor in the center, project files on the left, the assistant on the right and CI below.

7
00:00:28.054 --> 00:00:33.080
Open a file, edit its source or compare a split diff.

8
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:38.563
Inspect the failed test, ask for a fix and review the patch.

9
00:00:38.563 --> 00:00:42.218
Passing checks and approval are required before merging.

10
00:00:42.218 --> 00:00:44.503
This is a local simulation.

11
00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:46.269
Guide is optional.

12
00:00:46.269 --> 00:00:50.487
Its four steps cover palettes, motion settings and source locations.

13
00:00:50.487 --> 00:00:53.441
Back and Next keep the frame stable.

14
00:00:53.441 --> 00:00:58.503
Close it at any time, then reopen it from the top bar.

15
00:00:59.003 --> 00:01:01.504
Foundations contains the shared tokens.

16
00:01:01.504 --> 00:01:05.004
Inspect colors, type, spacing, radii and shadows.

17
00:01:05.004 --> 00:01:09.505
The tuning panel changes the interface palette and appearance.

18
00:01:09.505 --> 00:01:12.505
Mono keeps chart series in color.

19
00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.211
Replay or scrub an easing curve.

20
00:01:15.211 --> 00:01:18.153
Change the spring parameters and compare the result.

21
00:01:18.153 --> 00:01:22.197
Full, slow and reduced motion are available in the tuning panel.

22
00:01:22.197 --> 00:01:25.507
System reduced motion is respected unless Full is selected.

23
00:01:26.007 --> 00:01:31.123
Search the icon registry, adjust size and stroke, or play the collection.

24
00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:33.681
Each icon has its own animation.

25
00:01:33.681 --> 00:01:39.650
The same registry is used in navigation, controls, drag handles and coding-workspace tool results.

26
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:43.835
These controls show pending, success and failure states.

27
00:01:43.835 --> 00:01:46.138
Retry the failed local action.

28
00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:49.362
A hold can be cancelled before completion.

29
00:01:49.362 --> 00:01:53.507
Its confirmation time stays the same under reduced motion.

30
00:01:53.507 --> 00:01:57.652
Tabs, chips and menus also work with a keyboard.

31
00:01:58.152 --> 00:02:03.274
Expand a panel, then drag files between the pinned and unpinned groups.

32
00:02:03.274 --> 00:02:06.262
Sort tasks with a pointer or keyboard.

33
00:02:06.262 --> 00:02:10.957
Space picks up and drops an item; Escape restores its position.

34
00:02:10.957 --> 00:02:15.653
The remaining examples cover text changes, counters, flipping and expandable details.

35
00:02:16.153 --> 00:02:20.553
Switch menu content, filter collections and follow a breadcrumb path.

36
00:02:20.553 --> 00:02:24.512
Use arrow keys in the file tree or dock.

37
00:02:24.512 --> 00:02:28.032
Pagination and the carousel keep one active panel.

38
00:02:28.032 --> 00:02:34.192
The workspace form validates each step and preserves its fields when you go back.

39
00:02:34.692 --> 00:02:39.734
Forms includes native inputs, live validation, password controls and verification codes.

40
00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:42.484
Pasting a code fills the slots.

41
00:02:42.484 --> 00:02:46.151
The profile form saves locally for the demo.

42
00:02:46.151 --> 00:02:51.193
File progress is simulated and does not upload the selected file.

43
00:02:51.693 --> 00:02:57.238
The chart waits until it enters the viewport, then traces its finished shape.

44
00:02:57.238 --> 00:03:00.224
Changing the range starts a new draw.

45
00:03:00.224 --> 00:03:03.636
Inspect a day with the pointer or keyboard.

46
00:03:03.636 --> 00:03:06.195
The reference uses generated sample data.

47
00:03:06.695 --> 00:03:13.039
Hover a bucket to compare values, or pin it with a click or key.

48
00:03:13.039 --> 00:03:16.211
Legend items and donut arcs respond together.

49
00:03:16.211 --> 00:03:21.196
Progress rings show the remaining amount while retaining the target value.

50
00:03:21.696 --> 00:03:27.160
Filter accounts, sort columns and select a row by clicking its empty space.

51
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.682
The checkbox draws its selected state.

52
00:03:29.682 --> 00:03:34.305
Keyboard selection, pagination and a local CSV export are also available.

53
00:03:34.805 --> 00:03:38.341
Open a dialog, drawer or sheet.

54
00:03:38.341 --> 00:03:41.287
Native modality keeps focus inside.

55
00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:45.413
Escape closes it and restores the trigger.

56
00:03:45.413 --> 00:03:51.306
Other examples cover menus, tooltips, accordions, toasts and loading states.

57
00:03:51.806 --> 00:03:55.032
Color and Mono both support light and dark.

58
00:03:55.032 --> 00:03:57.048
Theme transitions include the background.

59
00:03:57.048 --> 00:03:59.468
Preferences are saved in browser storage.

60
00:03:59.468 --> 00:04:04.307
The command palette opens pages and settings without resetting their local state.

61
00:04:04.807 --> 00:04:08.372
Download the standalone HTML file or clone the source.

62
00:04:08.372 --> 00:04:12.333
The quick start lists the reusable files and their dependencies.

63
00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:14.313
The web reference is implemented.

64
00:04:14.313 --> 00:04:17.482
React, SwiftUI and Rust adapters are not included.
